<!--
  BlockML Core — bootstrap documentation

  FQN: org.blockml.bml.documentation.ImplicitNamespaceResolution
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/schema/block"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/schema/block https://blockml.org/schemas/core/block.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.documentation">

  <idea>Context-bound implicit namespace for unqualified block references.</idea>

  <documentation>
    Unqualified block references are supported only at specialized, semantically unambiguous
    reference sites. Each site defines exactly one implicit namespace. The name expands directly:

    &lt;Name&gt; → &lt;implicitNamespace&gt;.&lt;Name&gt;

    There is no multi-stage search, no global TypeRegistry fallback, and no document-scope
    heuristics. If the expanded FQN does not exist or the Block does not satisfy the expected
    base type for that site, the compiler emits an error.

    Reference sites and implicit namespaces:
    • Property type → org.blockml.bml.type.*
    • Capability inputType / outputType → org.blockml.bml.type.*
    • Implementation language attribute → org.blockml.bml.language.*
    • status element content · bml:status attribute → org.blockml.bml.status.*
    • Capability type → org.blockml.bml.capability.*
    • Constraint validation attribute → org.blockml.bml.validation.*

    Examples:
    • &lt;width type="Integer" /&gt; → org.blockml.bml.type.Integer
    • &lt;implementation language="TypeScript"&gt; → org.blockml.bml.language.TypeScript
    • &lt;status&gt;Draft&lt;/status&gt; → org.blockml.bml.status.Draft
    • type="Transformation" on Capability → org.blockml.bml.capability.Transformation
    • validation="Error" on constraint → org.blockml.bml.validation.Error

    General block references have no implicit namespace — baseType, aggregation type,
    association type, and composition instance tags require a full FQN or xmlns prefix.
    Explicit FQNs and xmlns prefixes remain valid everywhere, including at specialized sites.
  </documentation>

  <references>
    <see file="02_mbml.md">
      Context-Bound Implicit Namespace — authoritative authoring rules.
    </see>
    <see file="00_bom_core.md">
      Context-bound implicit namespace summary.
    </see>
    <see block="doc:BmlNamespace">
      Mandatory domain.bml namespace — FQN layout.
    </see>
  </references>

  <name>ImplicitNamespaceResolution</name>
  <type>doc:ImplicitNamespaceResolution</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>

</block>
